{
  "id": "r09",
  "text": "Then came another test of the assumption that a digital library moves forward with you. In twenty twenty, reviewers reported playing P.T. on early PlayStation Five review hardware. For a short time, the old teaser appeared to have made the jump. In the days that followed, the listing changed to say it was playable on PlayStation Four, and the newer console would no longer run it. Sony told Polygon that the change was a publisher decision. These are historical reports about review hardware in twenty twenty, not a guide to what any workaround does today. They show the problem clearly enough: a newer machine did not guarantee a permanent route back. The age of your hardware and the survival of an experience had become connected in a way a download button never really explains.",
